; `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` declares a peer range ending at ESLint 9 but runs
; correctly on the ESLint 10 this project uses, and several `@medplum/*` and
; Google Cloud packages pin older React/peer ranges. Without this flag a fresh
; `npm install` aborts on those ranges even though the resolved tree in
; package-lock.json is the one that has been tested. Set here rather than in
; CI alone so contributors and CI install the identical tree.
legacy-peer-deps=true
